## 7. If your teacher wants “round to nearest, half away from zero”

Here is a version without using `Math.round`:

```java
public int average(int[] array) {
    if (array.length == 0) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("Cannot average an empty array");
    }

    long sum = 0;
    for (int value : array) {
        sum += value;
    }

    long count = array.length;

    long quotient = sum / count;   // Java integer division: truncates toward zero
    long remainder = sum % count;  // same sign as sum

    long absRemainder = Math.abs(remainder);

    // If the fractional part is at least half, move away from zero.
    if (2 * absRemainder >= count) {
        if (sum > 0) {
            return (int) (quotient + 1);
        } else if (sum < 0) {
            return (int) (quotient - 1);
        }
    }

    return (int) quotient;
}
```

